<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prataparudra Deva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1497">1497</a>–<a href="/years/1540">1540</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prataparudra Deva was the last great ruler of the Gajapati Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> and the Bengal Sultanate, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnadevaraya">Krishnadevaraya</a> took his southern provinces. A devotee of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagannath">Jagannath</a>, he hosted the saint Chaitanya at Puri. Soon after his death his minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/govinda-vidyadhara">Govinda Vidyadhara</a> killed his heirs and founded the Bhoi dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prataparudra-deva.jpg" alt="Prataparudra Deva" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Manjit Keshari Nayak · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gajapati_Prataprudra_Deva.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
